            "This is caused by missing handling of PSS signatures in rsa_setup_md() in the signature provider code for rsa.",
            "After correcting `obj_xref.txt` to map `rsassaPss` to sig alg `rsassaPss`, I came across another bug:\r\n```\r\napps/openssl verify -auth_level 1 -purpose sslserver -trusted test/certs/root-cert.pem -untrusted test/certs/ca-cert.pem test/certs/ee-pss-sha256-cert.pem\r\nCN = PSS-SHA256\r\nerror 68 at 0 depth lookup: CA signature digest algorithm too weak\r\nerror test/certs/ee-pss-sha256-cert.pem: verification failed\r\n```\r\nwhich is because `rsa_pss_asn1_meth` did not include `rsa_sig_info_set`.\r\nI'm fixing this as well in #13982.",
